    "3: AXIS2-SECOND-LOOP phase-2 — s3_resource_alloc.py extended: DEBOUNCE_BASELINE=3, MAX_DEBOUNCE=15, AGGREGATE_STEP=2. _aggregate_phi_up() buffers phi_up events within widened debounce window, emits summaries on flush. observe_divergence() widened debounce alongside admit_rate attenuation. REVERT restores debounce to baseline. Both compose: debounce aggregates input variety, admit_rate dampens amplifier. R4 atomic deploy to LXC 101: PID 2260727 running (1131 lines). Phase-2 symbols verified (16 occurrences of new constants/methods).",
  ],
  findings: [
    "Real gap is 40, not 67. Only secondary continental stations need calibration; grid points (ENSO/PSO/HUM) are exogenous drivers. Original census denominator was inflated by counting data sources as viable subsystems.",
    "The 10 primary continentals + 3 island stations were calibrated because they're the original v1 set (before the v2 expansion to 80 nodes). The 40 secondary continentals are the v2 additions that never got the ERA5 sweep.",
    "Debounce window widening (aggregation) is structurally correct: within a widened window, repeated identical regime ticks collapse into one summary with count. A real regime change triggers an early flush (regime change detection). This is lossless of SIGNAL but collapses redundant chatter — Beer's Cyberfilter.",
