session("2026-07-13-ds-v2") = {
  summary:  "P1 incident root cause CORRECTED: not OOM but HOST CPU STARVATION (7.76 load on 2 cores). L1: cpulimit=1 on 110. L2: KEEP_ALIVE=5m. A0 switched to 1.5b. L4: OLLAMA_TIMEOUT=200s. Nucleus stable NRestarts=0, host load 3.32.",
  result:   pass,
  resolved: [
    "OLLAMA-110-RESIZE — pct set 110 --memory 8192. Corrected: 4GB→8GB was necessary (7B fits) but exposed the real root cause — both models now loaded, 2-core CPU saturated.",
    "L1 (CPU budget) — pct set 110 --cpulimit 1. Host load dropped from 7.76→3.32. Root cause relief confirmed.",
    "L2 (single model) — OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=-1→5m in /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service on LXC 110. Restarted with R4. Only 1.5b runner resident (7B unloaded after idle timeout).",
    "L2b (model assignment) — vsf-a0-classifier was requesting 7B from LXC 110 every 300s, competing with nucleus's 1.5b on same 1-core cap. Switched A0 to 1.5b (Environment=OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:1.5b). Backup at .bak.",
    "L4 (functional timeout) — OLLAMA_TIMEOUT restored from 20s→200s in /root/nucleus-wrapper.sh. Previous values: 20s→90s→150s→180s→200s. S4 cycle completes in ~200s on 1 core (num_predict=150 bottleneck).",
    "Nucleus restarted 4× with R4 (stop→verify PID gone→start→verify active). NRestarts=0 since last deploy.",
  ],
  findings: [
    "TRUE ROOT CAUSE: SIGKILL was HOST CPU STARVATION, not OOM and not watchdog. n02 is 2-core i7-7600U (4 threads). LXC 110 had NO cpulimit, KEEP_ALIVE=-1 pinned 7B+1.5b both resident with concurrent inference → host load 7.76 (~388% sat). The nucleus's tokio watchdog task (2 worker threads) couldn't be scheduled → 3 missed keepalives → SIGKILL. Confirmed: 'code=killed, status=9/KILL' after 1s (last telemetry 00:30:43, SIGKILL 00:30:44) — too fast for watchdog (30s gap needed).",
    "The 20s client timeout helped the DIRECT path (S4 call doesn't block) but not the INDIRECT path (CPU starvation). And it left S4 always-timeouting.",
    "L1 (cpulimit=1 on 110) + L2 (single 1.5b resident) dropped host load from 9.30→3.32 within minutes.",
    "The 1.5b model on 1 core with num_ctx=256, num_predict=150 takes ~200s for the nucleus's system-state prompt. OLLAMA_TIMEOUT=200s barely misses. Fix: reduce num_predict to ~80 (tokens/second ≈ 1 for 1.5B on 1 core).",
    "A0 classifier (vsf-a0-classifier on LXC 101) was also targeting LXC 110 ollama with 7B every 300s. With both models on 1 core, neither completes. Switched A0 to 1.5b as temp measure. Claude decides model assignment (open_q in spec).",
    "S4 is structurally mis-coupled for this hardware: blocking ureq calls on a 1-core CPU cap produce ~200s latency per cycle. The true fix is L3 (dedicated watchdog OS thread) + reduced num_predict.",
  ],
  commits:  [
    "22e694c — fix(incident): W3-OLLAMA-MIGRATE — resize LXC 110 to 8GB, reduce ollama timeout to 20s",
    "pending — this session block + corrected root cause + L1+L2+L4 changes",
  ],
  verify:   [
